  "rule": "manifest_version 3: signed preimage = P(\"seam.audit.chain-manifest.v3\") || P(stream_id) || P(tenant) || P(governing_doc_sha256) || P(le64 governing_generated_at) || P(le64 manifest_at) || P(le32 count) || per chain {P(flow_id) || P(env) || V || P(le64 len) || P(head) || P(le32 state) || B(batch_boundary)} || P(issuer_aid) || P(le32 digest_schema) || P(le64 tenant_len) || P(tenant_head) || B(tenant_batch_boundary), where B(x) = P(\"\") when x is null, else P(le64 x): the chain's S-3 history boundary (the position of its first Merkle batch entry) when below len, else null. manifest_version 0 (sealed before the boundary): the same without every B(..) under P(\"seam.audit.chain-manifest.v2\"); its boundaries are null. signature = Ed25519(SHA-256(preimage)); entry digest = SHA-256(P(\"seam.audit.chain-manifest-entry.v1\") || P(preimage) || P(signature)). Structural refusals before the signature: chains_not_ascending (strictly ascending by flow_id then env, both bytewise, then version numerically), a ChainKey rule for a malformed (flow_id, env, version), state_unknown (not 1..=4), empty_head_not_genesis (len 0 and head != genesis(K)), boundary_not_below_len (a boundary >= its len). A holder that walks a listed chain checks the walk switches to batches exactly at its boundary. state: 1 active, 2 retired, 3 moved_out, 4 destroyed. The event is a CHAIN_MANIFEST on the tenant chain (tag 30 payload, tag 29 kind 1) whose prev is tenant_head at position tenant_len (D-163: a verified manifest covers the tenant chain up to that head).",
